        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0644" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg556"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 426.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The refusal of the provincial authorities
                    to issue a permit to Mr. Bartlett for the completion of his building at Bourdour
                    was communicated to the Department December 17, 1891 (No. 364). Information <pb
                        facs="0645" n="557" xml:id="pg557"/> of the continued refusal of the
                    authorities to issue the required permit has just been filed with the legation,
                    in consequence of which I addressed a note to the Sublime Porte (copy
                    inclosed—No. 1).</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d427-a1.xml" xpointer="d427-a1"/>
            </div>
